# oracle: pair_style mliap model linear with descriptor ace on three elements: the H_N_O_ccs.yace descriptors of the LAMMPS example examples/mliap (91 per element) with constructed linear coefficients, on that example's 161-atom H/N/O cell (ace_compute_struct.data), run 0 then 4 NVE steps
# Native reference: LAMMPS b332f28 built with PKG_ML-IAP, PKG_ML-SNAP and PKG_ML-PACE (the installed binary has no ML-PACE)
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native: thermo 1.4e-13, atoms 3.9e-15.
# oracle-inputs: w277ma_HNO_linear.mliap.model
# oracle-examples: mliap/H_N_O_ccs.yace mliap/ace_compute_struct.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p
atom_modify     map hash
read_data       ace_compute_struct.data
mass            1 1.00
mass            2 14.00
mass            3 15.999
pair_style      mliap model linear w277ma_HNO_linear.mliap.model descriptor ace H_N_O_ccs.yace
pair_coeff      * * H N O
thermo_style    custom step pe press pxx pyy pzz pxy pxz pyz
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
fix             1 all nve
timestep        0.0001
thermo          2
run             4
